{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779507922,"nonce":"RAjxuzab3LnGjN5s930iRZHppiw=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ8kIg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/169","origin":"github"},"title":"Data analysis umbrella for #160 (2026-05-22 deployment) — standard checklist + sub-issue tracker","message":"## Goal\n\nUmbrella tracker for **post-mission analysis** of the [2026-05-22 deployment (#160)](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/160). Two layers:\n\n1. **Standard per-deployment analyses** (proposed convention, defined here; if the shape proves itself we promote it into [`docs/logs/README.md`](../blob/jazzy/docs/logs/README.md) as a documented wrap-up step).\n2. **#160-specific deep-dives** (already filed as their own issues; tracked here for completion).\n\nPurpose: make sure none of this slips. By June 4 (dev freeze) we want the class-prep-relevant outputs in hand.\n\n## Bag data inventory\n\n- **Bag DB**: `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-22_deployment.db` (1.9 GB, 4.18 M messages; already extracted from `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-05-22T21-05-06+00-00` which covers 17:05:07 → 20:34:23 EDT — pre-launch dockside through ~22 min of post-recovery charging)\n- **Launch/recovery times** already detected: launch 17:28:52 EDT, recovery 20:12:18 EDT, in-water 2h 43m 26s\n- **Source bags + per-host logs** under `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/`, `~/data/logs/bizzyboat_sonar/`, `~/data/logs/bizzy_images/`, `~/data/logs/operator/2026-05-22/`\n- **gabby boot history**: [`bizzyboat_project11/docs/gabby_boot_history_2026-05-15_to_2026-05-22.md`](../blob/jazzy/bizzyboat_project11/docs/gabby_boot_history_2026-05-15_to_2026-05-22.md) — power-cycle ground truth\n- **Dev + per-host logs**: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_{dev,gabby,salmon}_logs.md`\n\n## Quick-start: run the bag-analysis report\n\n`marine_tools/bag_analysis` has a one-command tier-1 report renderer that produces summary.md + PNG plots covering altitude/heave, comms, mode timeline, power, sensor health, speed/heading, and track:\n\n```bash\nsource /home/roland/project11/layers/main/sensors_ws/install/setup.bash\nros2 run bag_analysis sqlite_to_report \\\n  --db ~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-22_deployment.db \\\n  --output ~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-22/report\n```\n\nThat's the starting point — run it first, read the auto-generated summary.md, then drill in on whatever each plot surfaces against the standard-checklist items below.\n\n## Standard per-deployment analyses (proposed convention)\n\n- [ ] **Tier-1 bag_analysis report** — `sqlite_to_report` output (command above). Captures the foundation: altitude/heave, comms, mode timeline, power, sensor health, speed/heading, track plots.\n- [ ] **Mission timeline reconstruction** — launch/recovery (✅ already pinned), mission state transitions (`/bizzy/marine/status/mission_manager`), mode transitions (`/bizzy/mavros/state`), hover engagement events, autonomy-vs-manual phase windows. Output: per-phase timestamp table.\n- [ ] **Topic completeness check** — every topic in `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`'s recording list actually recorded? Flag absent topics + any with anomalous message rates vs. expected.\n- [ ] **Bag integrity** — message-format errors, time-gap anomalies (gaps \u003e N seconds in steady-state topics), time-sync sanity (sysfixtime / NTP boundaries don't leave invalid timestamps).\n- [ ] **Tide / chart-datum chain plausibility** — `/bizzy/tide_estimate`, `/bizzy/mllw_offset`, `/bizzy/mhhw_offset` recorded valid values across the mission. `map → map_tide` TF healthy at expected rate. PR #153 follow-up validation.\n- [ ] **Survey-pattern execution** — planned trackline vs. actual track per survey loop, XTE per line, line completion rate, dwell time per line, turn-apron behavior. Feeds [#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164).\n- [ ] **Link statistics summary** — udp_bridge per-topic rates, resend counts, give-up counters, WiFi vs Starlink + VPN path utilization. Class-planning input.\n- [ ] **Diagnostics summary** — health snapshot at key milestones (pre-launch, launch, mid-mission, recovery). Escalations during mission. Time-in-ERROR per source. Cross-correlate with operator-side annunciator state.\n- [ ] **Notable events extraction** — cross-correlate per-host log entries (operator observations from `2026-05-22_dev_logs.md`, gabby + salmon entries) with bag timestamps. Produces the \"narrative + data\" record for posterity.\n- [ ] **Findings register** — durable observations (positive + negative) consolidated from the above. Feed back to [`docs/roadmap.md`](../blob/jazzy/docs/roadmap.md) for any class-prep updates.\n\n## #160-specific deep-dives (filed as sub-issues)\n\n- [ ] [#167](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/167) **Comprehensive cross-deployment power-usage analysis** — chained 2026-05-19 → 21 → 22 single-charge-cycle dataset. 4 sub-analyses: cross-deployment battery model + recharge curve · voltage-sag-vs-SOC · speed-power model · phase-by-phase draw. Class-planning numbers.\n- [ ] [#168](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/168) **Survey efficiency** — coverage-area-per-energy from today's mission patterns. Sister analysis to #167.\n- [ ] [#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164) **SE undulation** — bag analysis: XTE per direction, `cmd_vel.linear.y` sign distribution, thruster-output asymmetry check if available.\n- [ ] [#165](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/165) **Hover drift** — per-event analysis table across multiple hover engagements today.\n- [ ] [#166](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/166) **CAMP freeze** — operator-side log post-mortem ([scope-addition comment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/166#issuecomment-4524043415)) covering both events.\n\n## Deliverable shape\n\nA unified `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-22/findings.md` (mirroring the 2026-05-01 precedent) combining:\n\n- Auto-generated tier-1 report (sqlite_to_report output)\n- Per-item findings against the standard checklist above\n- Links to sub-issue outcomes as they're addressed\n\n## Class-prep timeline\n\n**Hard deadline**: useful outputs by **June 4** (dev freeze). The class-blocking items ([#162](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/162) annunciator, [#163](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/163) AML probe) have their own paths to resolution; this umbrella is about the analysis layer underneath them.\n\nSub-issue parallelism is possible (different analyses can be done by different agents against the shared bag DB). The standard checklist items are largely independent — pick whichever surfaces useful findings fastest.\n\n## Convention promotion\n\nIf the standard-checklist shape proves itself on #160, promote it into [`docs/logs/README.md`](../blob/jazzy/docs/logs/README.md) as a documented wrap-up step (post-mission analysis section, after the existing wrap-up checklist). Cross-reference workspace [`rolker/ros2_agent_workspace#477`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace/issues/477) (the workspace-level deployment-logging capability tracker).\n\nPart of #160.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}